  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 152 PM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nAs of 145 PM Thursday afternoon, deep midlevel troughing \nremains across the eastern CONUS with ridging across the west. \nThis places the central Plains within a northwesterly midlevel \nflow pattern. A speed max was translating through Ozark region, \nresulting a few midlevel clouds across the eastern half of the \nstate. At the surface, an expansive surface ridge axis extends \nfrom eastern ND through eastern OK. This is yielding in light \nwinds across the region and temperatures in the 50s to near 60.\n\nBeyond Thursday, midlevel ridging will slide across the Plains ahead \nof the next midlevel trough across the west. This trough axis is \nexpected to eject into the central/southern Plains late Saturday \ninto Sunday. Latest deterministic and ensemble guidance continue to \ntrend towards a weaker trough/low with a more-southern track across \nOK. This trend will need to be monitored over the coming days as the \nprospects for widespread rainfall may be decreasing. Transitioning \ninto next week, an active midlevel pattern may emerge with multiple \nstorm systems potentially impacting the central Plains. The first \nshortwave trough may arrive towards the middle of next week with a \nsecond towards the following weekend.",
